{"author":{"id":"038d65070aa747b6bc9d50939fa697ec871a40ed259db54429b255bbef2581d6"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1793372910,"nonce":"TkDN9m9ksUhjN4LkNo/ScfznhRA=","message":"Spike measurements (2026-10-30). Code: src/rayde/preview/SurfaceProtocol.hx (the seed of this protocol: length-prefixed records HELLO, FRAME with a damage rectangle and a raw or deflated payload, LOG, EXIT, INPUT), tests/surface/SurfaceProducer.hx (a synthetic software app) and tests/surface/SurfaceSpike.hx (the viewer and the measurements). 1280x720 RGBA, 90 frames paced at 30 fps, producer and viewer on one machine, the session variant through a real rayde-session over WebSocket.\n\n| transport | scene | encoding | KB per frame | Mbit/s at 30 fps | viewer decode ms |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| local | ui (small box over a page) | raw | 123.8 | 30.4 | 0.25 |\n| local | ui | deflate | 2.2 | 0.5 | 2.04 |\n| local | game (whole picture scrolls) | raw | 3600 | 884.7 | 0.93 |\n| local | game | deflate | 83.0 | 20.4 | 24.57 |\n| local | noise (every pixel changes) | raw | 3600 | 884.7 | 4.64 |\n| local | noise | deflate | 3600 (deflate failed or did not help) | 884.7 | 4.57 |\n| session | ui | raw | 123.8 | 30.4 | 0.09 |\n| session | ui | deflate | 2.2 | 0.5 | 1.69 |\n| session | game | raw | 3600 | 884.7 | 1.45 |\n\nThe last three session rows (game deflate, noise) were cut off by the harness's 10-minute limit. The bytes through a session equal the bytes locally: the session adds base64 and JSON on top, which this table does not include.\n\nWhat the numbers support:\n- Damage rectangle plus deflate makes UI-like content negligible (2.2 KB a frame, 0.5 Mbit/s at 30 fps). A tools or application preview is cheap.\n- Full-screen motion deflated losslessly is 83 KB a frame, 20 Mbit/s at 30 fps: too much for a WAN link; it needs a video codec or lossy tiles. Incompressible content (noise, or video-like scenes) cannot be lossless at all: raw is 885 Mbit/s.\n- Ash's built-in deflate fails on incompressible data (\"Compression failed\" on 3.7 MB of noise). A producer must choose the encoding per frame, falling back to raw when deflate fails or is not smaller; the spike's producer does, and the protocol allows it.\n- A Haxe viewer inflating a 3.6 MB frame took 24.6 ms: the page should inflate natively in the browser (DecompressionStream) or decode a codec there, not in Haxe.\n\nWhat the numbers do not support: the fps and input-latency columns of the spike's output are the synthetic producer's own speed (it fills 0.9 million pixels in a Haxe loop, about a second a frame for full-screen scenes) and say nothing about transport. Real latency needs a producer that reads pixels back at native speed, a hosted session over a real link, and the browser path (ash-channel, not the native WebSocket client used here). Not measured: GPU upload per frame in a page, the Ash-in-MSB cost, or any real framework.","files":null}]}